       EVP_KDF-PKCS12KDF - The PKCS#12 EVP_KDF implementation

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Support for computing the PPKKCCSS##1122 password‐based KDF through the
       EEVVPP__KKDDFF API.

       The EVP_KDF-PKCS12KDF algorithm implements the PKCS#12 password‐based
       key derivation function, as described in appendix B of RFC 7292 (PKCS
       #12: Personal Information Exchange Syntax); it derives a key from a
       password using a salt, iteration count and the intended usage.

   IIddeennttiittyy
       "PKCS12KDF" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with
       the EEVVPP__KKDDFF__ffeettcchh(()) function.

   SSuuppppoorrtteedd ppaarraammeetteerrss
       The supported parameters are:

       "pass" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__PPAASSSSWWOORRDD) <octet string>
       "salt" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__SSAALLTT) <octet string>
       "iter" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__IITTEERR) <unsigned integer>
       "properties" (OOSSSSLL__KKDDFF__PPAARRAAMM__PPRROOPPEERRTTIIEESS) <UTF8 string>
